1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SPEAKERA: Blue scatters nearly six times more than red, so scattered blue reaches us from all over the sky.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SPEAKERB: Violet scatters even more, but sunlight holds less of it, and our eyes are less sensitive to it.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
SPEAKERA: At sunset, the light crosses so much air that the blue is scattered away, leaving orange and red.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
SPEAKERB: And clouds, made of far bigger droplets, scatter every colour alike, so they stay white.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
SPEAKERA: That's a lot of sky to explain with one small rule.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
SPEAKERB: Every patch of blue you see is sunlight that the air itself has turned toward your eyes.
